many ccsd teachers are facing problems  when it comes to health insurance like  being able to find a provider or simply  have their bills covered sally jaramillo  live in the newsroom tonight sally you  spoke to some of those teachers what are  they telling you  yes i did some teachers didn't want to  be identified but they tell me these  issues with their insurance have gotten  worse over the last couple of months  this all starting since the end of last  year today they simply want to receive  the benefits they deserve  i think there are a lot of issues that  not only myself but other teachers some  teachers are having trouble finding a  doctor others having trouble getting  elective surgeries covered by their  health insurance luanne wagner has been  a teacher for 24 years and says in her  entire career she's never seen anything  like this my situation  i'm i'm paying for the preferred  provider insurance for my dental  and then out of the blue i found out  through my dentist office that i've been  switched to an hmo wagner says she's in  shock over the change i was told as  there was a glitch in the system  people's insurances got switched but  then for us to get it switched back  we're being told that we have to file an  appeal this is extremely difficult for  her and her family her husband needing a  dental procedure now if we have to pay  out of pocket it's going to be over a  thousand dollars patrick cassell is an  insurance broker with multi-care group  he's been servicing the state of nevada  for over 30 years and says the school  district health problems have been going  on for decades depending on who the  carrier is and depending on how things  are being set up it can be very  difficult to get access to a doctor in  less than 90 days casell also added the  solution could be pretty simple and open  up their own medical clinics  strategically throughout the valley if  they did that then then all their people  would have access to seeing doctors  quicker and all wagner wants our  benefits  need to improve  casell adds there's no excuse to receive  a bill and not have access to someone  who can't explain what the problems are  i also reached out to the school  district about this they share some  background information on how ccsd is  working to have tht health be open and  honest that link can be found on our  website 8newsnow.com reporting from the  newsroom sally jaramillo live local now
 

